! **The one-shot leg of `co-helix4-nosoc.in`, with spin-orbit coupling**: the same
! four-cell cobalt helix on the fully-relativistic `Co.rel-pbe-nd-rrkjus.UPF` of the
! same generation, diagonalised once at the source's density turned by a rotation
! (`run_orientation_torque`). Everything but the dataset and the coupling is the
! source's, as the two-file route requires.
&control
   calculation = 'nscf'
/
&system
   ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 4.60, celldm(3) = 5.20, nat = 4, ntyp = 4,
   noncolin = .true., lspinorb = .true., lforcet = .true., nosym = .true., ecutwfc = 20.0, ecutrho = 160.0,
   occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'mv', degauss = 0.02,
   starting_magnetization(1) = 0.6, angle1(1) = 90.0, angle2(1) = 0.0,
   starting_magnetization(2) = 0.6, angle1(2) = 90.0, angle2(2) = 90.0,
   starting_magnetization(3) = 0.6, angle1(3) = 90.0, angle2(3) = 180.0,
   starting_magnetization(4) = 0.6, angle1(4) = 90.0, angle2(4) = 270.0,
/
&electrons
   conv_thr = 1.0e-9
   mixing_beta = 0.3
/
ATOMIC_SPECIES
Co1 58.933 Co.rel-pbe-nd-rrkjus.UPF
Co2 58.933 Co.rel-pbe-nd-rrkjus.UPF
Co3 58.933 Co.rel-pbe-nd-rrkjus.UPF
Co4 58.933 Co.rel-pbe-nd-rrkjus.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
Co1 0.0 0.0 0.00
Co2 0.0 0.0 0.25
Co3 0.0 0.0 0.50
Co4 0.0 0.0 0.75
K_POINTS automatic
3 3 1 0 0 1
